---
seoTitle: "SCIPS: support for tenants, residents and community groups in Sandwell"
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Home
description: "SCIPS is a community-led charity in West Bromwich helping tenants, residents and community groups across Sandwell have a say on their homes and neighbourhoods."
heroPhoto: "6815366"
tasks:
  - title: Start a residents' group
    desc: Bring neighbours together and set your group up properly
    url: /residents-groups/#starting
    photo: "7398084"
  - title: Support for your group
    desc: Constitutions, meetings, AGMs, money and funding
    url: /residents-groups/#running
    photo: "6351591"
  - title: Have your say on housing
    desc: Forums, panels and groups that residents can join
    url: /get-involved/
    photo: "5220886"
  - title: Training
    desc: Skills to run meetings and represent your area
    url: /how-we-help/#training
    photo: "5853324"
  - title: Help with an issue
    desc: Raise a problem with the people who can fix it
    url: /how-we-help/#advocacy
    photo: "5371532"
  - title: Talk to someone
    desc: Not sure where to start? Call or send us a message
    url: /contact/
    photo: "7470106"
situations:
  - label: Group support
    quote: Bins, fly-tipping, broken lights. You've reported it again and again and nothing changes.
    how: We help neighbours raise issues together as a group, so they reach the right people and get a proper answer.
  - label: Starting a group
    quote: You want to start a residents' group but have no idea where to begin.
    how: We'll take you through it from the first meeting to a constitution, committee and bank account.
  - label: Consultation
    quote: Your group has been asked for its views on a housing plan and the paperwork is a lot.
    how: We explain what's being asked in plain English and help you get your group's response in.
  - label: Training
    quote: You've just become chair or treasurer and nobody has shown you what to do.
    how: Training for committee members and volunteers, so you feel confident in the role.
  - label: Building safety
    quote: You live in a high-rise block and have questions about fire, gas or water safety.
    how: We can point you to the Resident Building Safety Forum and help you put your questions.
  - label: Advocacy
    quote: Something isn't right with your home and you don't feel listened to.
    how: We help you set out your case clearly and take it to the people who can put it right.
places:
  - { id: "5290424", name: "West Bromwich", note: "Our office is here, on Birmingham Road" }
  - { id: "7457170", name: "Smethwick" }
  - { id: "6815409", name: "Tipton" }
  - { id: "7476781", name: "Wednesbury" }
  - { id: "6345055", name: "Tividale" }
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import arrow %}

{# 1. Hero: a house window you scroll through until the street fills the screen #}
<section class="xh" data-cursor="Scroll" data-scene="hero" data-theme="dark" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="xh__stage">
    <div class="xh__frame" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="xh__window" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="xh__photo">{% picture heroPhoto, "100vw", { loading: "eager", widths: [800, 1024] } %}</div>
      <span class="xh__bars"></span>
    </div>

    <p class="xh__kicker">Community-led charity · Borough of Sandwell</p>
    <h1 id="hero-title" class="xh__title">
      <span class="xh__half xh__half--l">Your home.</span>
      <span class="xh__half xh__half--r">Your say.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="xh__lede">We help tenants, residents and community groups across Sandwell come together, get organised and be heard.</p>
    <p class="xh__hint" aria-hidden="true"><span></span>Scroll</p>

    <div class="xh__after">
      <p class="xh__statement">Helping Sandwell residents have a say in their homes and neighbourhoods.</p>
      <div class="button-group">
        <a class="button button--brand" href="/residents-groups/">Start a residents' group {{ arrow() | safe }}</a>
        <a class="button button--glass" href="/how-we-help/">How we help</a>
      </div>
      <p class="xh__credit credit">{% credit heroPhoto %}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# 2. Who we are: the statement lights up word by word as you scroll #}
<section class="xs curtain" data-scene="reveal" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <figure class="xs__float xs__float--a" data-speed="-0.18">
    {% picture "5783648", "(min-width: 60em) 18vw, 40vw" %}
    <figcaption class="credit">{% credit "5783648" %}</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure class="xs__float xs__float--b" data-speed="0.14">
    {% picture "6815381", "(min-width: 60em) 24vw, 50vw" %}
    <figcaption class="credit">{% credit "6815381" %}</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="container xs__inner">
    <h2 id="about-title" class="eyebrow">About SCIPS · Run by local people, for local people</h2>
    <p class="xs__text" data-words>SCIPS is a charity led and governed by the community. We help residents build pride in their neighbourhoods, and make sure their views reach the people who make decisions.</p>
    <dl class="xs__facts">
      <div><dt>Area</dt><dd>All six towns</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Referral</dt><dd>Not needed</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Charity no.</dt><dd><a href="{{ site.charityRegister }}">{{ site.charityNumber }}</a></dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="xs__more"><a class="arrow-link" href="/about/">More about us</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

{# 3. Ways in: a list of tasks beside a photo that changes with the one you point at #}
<section class="xt curtain" aria-labelledby="tasks-title" data-tasks>
  <div class="container xt__grid">
    <div class="xt__list">
      <h2 id="tasks-title" class="eyebrow">How can we help?</h2>
      <p class="xt__intro">Choose what you'd like to do. Not sure? <a href="tel:{{ site.phoneHref }}">Call us</a> and we'll talk it through.</p>
      <ol class="xt__rows">
        {% for t in tasks %}
        <li>
          <a class="xt__row" data-cursor="Open" href="{{ t.url }}" data-task="{{ loop.index0 }}">
            <span class="xt__num">{{ "0" + loop.index }}</span>
            <span class="xt__title">{{ t.title }}</span>
            <span class="xt__desc">{{ t.desc }}</span>
            <span class="xt__arrow">{{ arrow() | safe }}</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="xt__media" inert>
      <div class="xt__frame">
        {% for t in tasks %}
        <div class="xt__img{% if loop.first %} is-active{% endif %}" data-task-img="{{ loop.index0 }}">
          {% picture t.photo, "(min-width: 60em) 40vw, 1px" %}
          <span class="credit">{% credit t.photo %}</span>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# 4. Sound familiar? One situation at a time, held on screen while you scroll #}
<section class="xq curtain" data-scene="steps" data-theme="dark" aria-labelledby="situations-title" style="--n: {{ situations.length }}">
  <div class="xq__stage">
    <div class="container xq__grid">
      <div class="xq__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p>
        <h2 id="situations-title" class="xq__title" data-split>Things we can help with</h2>
        <div class="xq__progress" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="xq__count"><span data-step-current>01</span> / {{ "0" + situations.length }}</span>
          <span class="xq__bar"><span></span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="xq__list">
        {% for s in situations %}
        <li class="xq__item{% if loop.first %} is-active{% endif %}" data-step="{{ loop.index0 }}">
          <p class="xq__label">{{ s.label }}</p>
          <blockquote class="xq__quote"><p>{{ s.quote }}</p></blockquote>
          <p class="xq__how"><strong>How we help</strong> {{ s.how }}</p>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# 5. Where we work: full-screen places that stack over each other #}
<section class="xp" aria-labelledby="area-title">
  <div class="xp__intro" data-theme="dark">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="area-title" class="eyebrow">Where we work</h2>
      <p class="xp__lede">Across the whole borough. Our office is in West Bromwich, and we meet residents in local venues across Oldbury, Rowley Regis, Smethwick, Tipton and Wednesbury.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ol class="xp__list">
    {% for pl in places %}
    <li class="xp__panel" data-scene="panel" data-theme="dark">
      <figure>
        <div class="xp__img">{% picture pl.id, "100vw", { widths: [800, 1024] } %}</div>
        <figcaption>
          <span class="xp__index" aria-hidden="true">{{ "0" + loop.index }} / {{ "0" + places.length }}</span>
          <span class="xp__name">{{ pl.name }}</span>
          {% if pl.note %}<span class="xp__note">{{ pl.note }}</span>{% endif %}
          <span class="credit">{% credit pl.id %}</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

{# 6. Track record #}
<section class="xr curtain" data-scene="drift" data-theme="dark" aria-labelledby="strategy-title">
  <p class="xr__drift" aria-hidden="true"><span>Key partner · Key partner · Key partner · Key partner ·</span></p>
  <div class="container xr__grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Our track record</p>
      <h2 id="strategy-title" class="xr__title" data-split>We helped shape how Sandwell Council works with its tenants</h2>
      <p class="xr__body">The council's Tenant Engagement Strategy was written by a group of nine tenants, SCIPS and the council's housing team, working together.</p>
      <a class="button button--glass" href="{{ site.strategy }}">Read the strategy {{ arrow() | safe }}</a>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="xr__quote">
      <p>“…our key partner, Sandwell Community Information and Participation Services (SCIPS)”</p>
      <cite>Sandwell Council, Tenant Engagement Strategy</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

{# Town names, drifting #}
<div class="xm curtain" data-marquee aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="xm__track">
    {% for round in [1, 2] %}{% for town in ["West Bromwich", "Smethwick", "Tipton", "Wednesbury", "Oldbury", "Rowley Regis"] %}<span class="xm__item">{{ town }}<svg viewBox="0 0 40 40"><path d="M9 31V18.5L20 10l11 8.5V31h-7.5v-8h-7v8z"/></svg></span>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>

{# 7. Guides #}
<section class="xg" aria-labelledby="guides-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="xg__head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Free guides</p>
        <h2 id="guides-title" class="xg__title" data-split>Guides for residents' groups</h2>
      </div>
      <a class="arrow-link" href="/guides/">All guides</a>
    </div>
    <ol class="xg__list">
      {% for g in collections.guide | sort(false, false, "data.order") %}
      <li>
        <a class="xg__card" data-cursor="Read" href="{{ g.url }}">
          <span class="xg__num" aria-hidden="true">{{ "0" + loop.index }}</span>
          <strong>{{ g.data.title }}</strong>
          <span class="xg__sum">{{ g.data.summary }}</span>
          <span class="xg__meta">{{ g.data.readingTime }} read {{ arrow() | safe }}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{# 8. Contact #}
<section class="xc curtain" aria-labelledby="contact-title" data-hide-pill>
  <div class="container xc__grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Get in touch</p>
      <h2 id="contact-title" class="xc__title" data-split>Talk to us.</h2>
      <p class="xc__lede">You don't need a referral. Tell us what's happening where you live.</p>
      <a class="xc__phone" href="tel:{{ site.phoneHref }}">{{ site.phone }}</a>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Email</dt><dd><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Open</dt><dd>{{ site.hours }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Visit</dt><dd>{% for line in site.address %}{{ line }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="button-group mt-l"><a class="button" href="/contact/">Send us a message {{ arrow() | safe }}</a></div>
    </div>
    {% include "partials/map.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>
